INT. SUBWAY CAR - EVENING RUSH

A packed Number 6 train SCREECHES through the dark. Straphangers sway like seaweed. The lights flicker. The car smells of pizza and wet umbrellas.

CLOSE ON a tiny paper bag in the arms of POPPY NAKAMURA, 9, brave, braces on her teeth. Inside the bag, a hamster peeks out.

POPPY
Don't look, Biscuit. Crowds make you nervous.

BISCUIT (O.S.)
(muffled squeak)
I'm not nervous. You're nervous.

ANGLE ON Poppy's big brother, MARCUS, 15, headphones around his neck, glued to a dead phone.

MARCUS
Pop, we're four stops from home. Do not name-drop the hamster in public.

POPPY
He has a name, Marcus.

MARCUS
He has a name that means "snack" to every cat in Queens.

The train JERKS. Everybody lurches. A man's coffee flies.

WE SEE the lights die. Total black. A collective GASP.

The train GROANS to a stop.

POPPY (CONT'D)
Marcus?

MARCUS
Right here, Pop.

DELILAH
(from the dark, a big voice)
Everybody stay calm! I've been stuck down here before!

Poppy squints. A small flashlight clicks on. It shines on DELILAH OKONKWO, 60s, a transit worker's vest, a thermos the size of a fire hydrant.

DELILAH (CONT'D)
Ten minutes. Tops. Y'all hold hands if you gotta.

MARCUS
Is that official?

DELILAH
It's a suggestion, baby.

POPPY
Delilah, I think Biscuit's scared.

DELILAH
Biscuit is the hamster?

POPPY
He's a very brave hamster.

MARCUS
He is literally shaking.

POPPY
Marcus, shush!

DELILAH
Both of you shush. Hear that?

Silence. Then a faint CLANG, CLANG, CLANG from the tunnel ahead.

INSERT - THE TUNNEL WALL, a rusty pipe trembling.

POPPY
(whispering)
That's not a ten-minute noise.

DELILAH
(low)
No. It is not.

MARCUS
Okay. Okay. What do we do?

DELILAH
You and your sister stay by me. Poppy, you keep that little fella warm.

POPPY
(to the bag)
You hear that, Biscuit? We're a team now.

BISCUIT (O.S.)
(squeak)
Tell Marcus I said sorry about his sneakers.

MARCUS
What did he say?

POPPY
Nothing.

The clanging STOPS.

The lights flash on. The train LURCHES forward.

Everyone CHEERS.

BACK TO SCENE

Marcus slumps against a pole, laughing with relief. Poppy squeezes the bag. Delilah screws the cap on her thermos.

This is the last time the three of them will ever be strangers.

DELILAH
Next stop is yours, kids.

POPPY
Thank you, Delilah.

DELILAH
Thank the hamster.
